                <pb facs="0138" n="54" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg54"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay acknowledges Mr. Conger’s telegram of the 23d instant, and instructs him
                    to insist on the request of the United States for treaty ports and consulates in
                    Manchuria, and make our objections known to second clause, excluding all
                    foreigners but Russians from Chinese service. Discussion of other points is
                    reserved.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
